# LedgerLoop -- provider configuration.
#
# COPY THIS FILE TO `.env` AND FILL IN WHAT YOU HAVE. `.env` IS GITIGNORED.
# Nothing here is required: with none of these set, every command runs the whole
# pipeline deterministically and says so. `make eval` regenerates every published
# number with no key at all, and there is a test asserting that.
#
# These are read from the process environment, not from this file -- LedgerLoop
# adds no dotenv dependency. Load it however your shell prefers, e.g.
#
#   bash / zsh   set -a && . ./.env && set +a
#   PowerShell   Get-Content .env | ForEach-Object { if ($_ -match '^(\w+)=(.*)$') { Set-Item "env:$($Matches[1])" $Matches[2] } }

# --- the failover ladder -------------------------------------------------
# Tried in order; a rung with no credential is skipped. The first rung that
# answers is used, and how far down the run had to go is recorded in the cost
# ledger as `fallback_depth`, so a rate-limited run is visible rather than silent.
#
# `ollama` needs no key because it is a process on this machine. It is therefore
# the one rung that must be ASKED for -- either by naming it below or by setting
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL -- so that a machine with no credentials reaches the
# deterministic path immediately instead of waiting for localhost to time out.
# LEDGERLOOP_LLM_PROVIDERS=groq,gemini,openrouter,ollama

# --- per-provider keys ---------------------------------------------------
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# One key used by every rung that has no variable of its own. This is the
# Step 9 variable and it still works exactly as it did.
# LEDGERLOOP_LLM_API_KEY=

# --- optional endpoint overrides -----------------------------------------
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# GROQ_BASE_URL=
# GEMINI_BASE_URL=
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=
